# Odoo Development Pipeline

Pipeline orchestrator: manage the full dev lifecycle by spawning named subagents (defined in `.claude/agents/`), each specialized for a phase. Coordinate, pass context between phases, loop back on failure.

## Task

$ARGUMENTS

---

## Sessions: mother and child

A run is split over two sessions so that neither carries the other's context: the grill
and the ticket work stay out of the dev rounds, and the dev rounds stay out of the session
that deploys and closes.

| Session | Runs | Hands over |
|---------|------|------------|
| **mother** | Phase 0, Phase 1 (the task, what kb knows, the grill, the status, the ticket with test cases), then the brief and the child's start; afterwards the PR and CI check, the deploy on the user's command, Phase 7 | the brief |
| **child** | its own worktree env, Phase 2 dev, 3 QC gate, 4 docs{% if use_release_notes %}, 4b release note{% endif %}, 5 demo GIF, 6 PR, a session note | the report |

- **Which one is this session?** A child is started with a pipeline brief: its title starts
  with `[child] `, and it loads this skill with `child <TASK-KEYS>`. A child follows
  [Child session](#child-session) and skips Phase 0's kb task, Phase 1 and Phase 7. Every other
  start of this skill is a mother, or a single session (next point).
- **No session tool, one session.** When `mcp__ccd_session__start_session` is neither loaded
  nor listed as a deferred tool (terminal `claude`, a teammate without the desktop app), the whole pipeline runs in this one session, Phases 0 to 7 in order, as
  written below. Say so in one line ("No session tool here: the whole pipeline runs in this
  session.") and skip the hand-off.
- **Grouping is the mother's call.** Related tickets (the same module or the same files) go
  to ONE child: one worktree env, one PR. Independent tickets go to separate children,
  started in parallel, each with its own brief.
- **Questions go up, never sideways.** A child that meets an ambiguity asks the mother with
  `SendMessage` (the session that started it) and waits; it never guesses one of the user's
  decisions. The mother asks the user, records the answer on the ticket (a `Design Decision`
  note per `odoo-tickets`), and replies.
- **After the PR the mother forwards, the child fixes.** Review comments and CI failures on
  the PR go from the mother to the child that opened it (`SendMessage` to its session id);
  the child fixes them in its env and reports again.

