### Sub-tasks & Blockers (task↔task links)

Two task↔task link tabs the orchestrator maintains (fields + calls in
`odoo-tickets` → "Sub-tasks & blockers"). Both stay attached to the current
task — **distinct from OPEN_THREADS**, which are unrelated issues {% if use_kb %}the user
decides on, one by one, in Phase 7{% else %}that become standalone Backlog tasks in Phase 7{% endif %}.

- **Too big → Sub-task.** If you judge the task too large to ship as one clean
  PR (several independent deliverables, spans unrelated concerns), surface the
  proposed split to the **user first**, then create the agreed slices as child
  tasks (new `project.task`, `parent_id` = current task) and narrow this run's
  scope to one slice (or the parent's remaining work). Post a `Design Decision`
  note recording the split.
- **Blocker found → Blocked By.** If development or the QC gate hits a
  dependency that must be resolved first (missing upstream change, external
  fix, data migration), create a task for the blocker (full conventions) and
  link it on the current task's `depend_on_ids`. Post a `Progress` note naming
  the blocker, then take the **BLOCKED** close in Phase 7 — the current task
  can't finish until the blocker does.
- **Owner is not the user → handover note.** A slice, blocker or thread ticket
  created for someone else, or handed to them, gets the `odoo-tickets` handover
  note (draft shown to the user first, `mail.notification` read back).
