## Isolated per-session environment

Every run executes in its own isolated env — own worktree + port + DB + Odoo — so
parallel pipeline sessions never collide, and the user's checkout `src/{{ custom_repo_name }}`
is untouched; there is no main Odoo or main database to protect. **The model,
scripts and gotchas live in the `worktree-env` skill — read it.** What the pipeline
needs from it:

- **The session that develops** runs `wt-start.sh <slug>` (the child's first step; Phase 1
  step 8 in a single session) and captures its output as `<WT>` (worktree
  path), `<CONF>` (session `odoo.conf`), `<URL>` (browser URL), `<DB>`, `<PORT>`, and
  with `--env-repo` `<ENVREPO>` (this project's own repo on branch `<slug>`).
  Re-running `wt-start.sh <slug>` refreshes the env (idempotent). A mother never brings
  up an env of its own.
- **Phases 2–6** edit/test/PR using those: `git -C <WT> …`, `{{ odoo_cmd }} -c <CONF> …`,
  browser `<URL>`. All code/git happens in `<WT>`, never in `src/{{ custom_repo_name }}`.
- **Phase 7** does NOT tear the env down on its own — the worktree is kept so
  the task can continue. `wt-stop.sh <slug>` runs ONLY when the user says the
  session is finished, and only after you ask (see Phase 7 Step 0).
- A session is verified from its own conf: `{{ odoo_cmd }} shell -c <CONF> --no-http` with a script
  on stdin (a given user: `with_user()`), or `psql -d <DB>` for plain reads. The Odoo
  connector is production only.
- Prereq: a seed dump in `backup/` ({% if backup_s3_bucket %}`nix run .#download-backup` to fetch/refresh{% else %}drop a `pg_dump -Fc` file in manually{% endif %}) —
  if `wt-start` reports none, ask the user to {% if backup_s3_bucket %}run it once{% else %}provide it{% endif %} first.

