## Error Handling

- If a subagent fails, report the error and ask whether to retry or abort
- An agent cut off by a usage limit is not resumed after the reset (its cache is gone): a
  fresh one gets a brief with where it stopped (`git -C <WT> status --short`, its last report)
- Max 3 fix rounds in the Phase 3 gate, then stop and report (Phase 3, Gate decision)
- Always restart this session's service (`odoo{{ service_suffix }}-wt@<slug>.service`) after validation;
  the user's `odoo{{ service_suffix }}.service` and other sessions are never stopped
- On abort, do Phase 7 memory closure but **keep the worktree** — do NOT run
  `wt-stop.sh`; the env stays so work can resume, and teardown waits for the
  user's explicit go (Phase 7 Step 0)
- A child that stops for good (a usage limit, a crash, a session the user stopped) is not
  revived by messages: the mother starts a fresh child with the same brief plus where the
  last one stopped (its last report, `git -C <WT> status --short` and `git -C <WT> log --oneline -5`).
  The env is reused: `wt-start.sh <slug>` is idempotent

## Reporting

After each phase: `Phase X/7: <Name> — <STATUS> + 1-2 sentence summary`

A child ends with the child report (see [Child session](#child-session)); the mother ends with
the final summary below, built from the child reports.

